    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioners/accused would submit that all the allegations made in the FIR are self-contradictory, false and baseless; that, the petitioners /accused never demanded dowry;\nthat, respondent no.2/complainant only for harassing and with ulterior motive falsely implicated entire family of the petitioner no.1/husband; that, even there are allegations against the married sister of petitioner no.1/husband, who is not residing with them.\n5. Issue notice to respondent no.2 through ordinary process and registered post, acknowledgement due as well as by email and WhatsApp, if available.\n6. Steps to be taken within three weeks.\n7.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 951,
      "end": 1604,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2869674563407898
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "Learned counsel for the State seeks and is granted time to file counter affidavit.",
